commit 2f920761a5d4d8826a7729f885fa3056f9aacd28
Author: James Willcox <james@newydatalab.com.au>
Date:   Mon Nov 23 07:48:32 2026 +1100

    Type-check every workspace; pin duckdb
    
    Only the web app had a tsconfig, so the API, core and gtfs had never
    been type-checked. They now share tsconfig.base.json (strict, noEmit,
    erasable syntax only), and `npm run typecheck` at the root checks all
    four workspaces.
    
    - Add tsconfig.base.json and a tsconfig.json for api, core and gtfs;
      web now extends the base with the same settings as before.
    - Fix 50 errors, with no change in behaviour: row types on queries
      (describe, platforms, vehicle days, the run library, playback stop
      times), a looser type for the who= query helper, @types/yauzl, and
      an await on the duckdb rows in export-check.
    - Pin @duckdb/node-api to 2.0.0-r.1, the version installed.
    - CLAUDE.md and /verify use the root typecheck.
    
    Tests: npm run typecheck, npm test (61 passed), npm run lint,
    prettier --check (end-of-line auto) passed; e2e suites not run.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

